                    "value": {
                      "kind": "scalar",
                      "value": "!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>\nFish\n# The Fish chapter — its own directory chapter. Positional body: prose, the `fish-tank.png`\n# image chunk (a sibling file here), and a PlantUML state diagram of the nitrogen cycle.\ndescription: A quiet window into another world\n- |\n  An aquarium is a small ecosystem, and **water quality is everything.**\n- *: fish-tank.png\n- |\n  Cycle a new tank for weeks before adding fish, so helpful bacteria can establish. Feed\n  sparingly: uneaten food fouls the water faster than anything else.\n- |\n  The bacteria you are waiting for run the **nitrogen cycle**, turning toxic waste into\n  something far milder:\n- !!<format: text/x-plantuml> |\n  @startuml\n  [*] --> Ammonia : fish waste\n  Ammonia --> Nitrite : Nitrosomonas\n  Nitrite --> Nitrate : Nitrobacter\n  Nitrate --> [*] : water change\n  @enduml\n\"fish-tank.png\":\n  .yo:\n    thumbnails:\n      [256, 256]: *: .yo: thumbnails: xxh64-09ea0c272066f155-256x256.jpg\n",
