            {
              "key": "body.yo",
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>\nThe Pet Keeper's Handbook\n# A recursive document tree (a pet-keeping handbook) where EACH chapter is its own directory.\n# This root's positional body interleaves prose (default markdown), an image chunk (`*png`\n# pointer — format from the .png extension), a PlantUML diagram (tagged `!!<format: …>`), and\n# three SUBCHAPTERS that are `*`-pointers to the `dogs/`, `cats/`, `fish/` subdirectories — each\n# its own directory chapter with its own `.yo/body.yo`. Spec: docs/documents/chapter, docs/language.\ndescription: A friendly guide to living with animals\n- |\n  **Pets share our homes, our routines, and a surprising amount of our furniture.** This\n  handbook collects what every keeper learns sooner or later, one species at a time.\n- |\n  Read the chapter for your companion, but the first rule is universal: *watch, listen, and\n  be patient.*\n- *: cover-paw.png\n- |\n  Three needs run through every chapter — **company, exercise, and a clean environment** —\n  weighted differently for each animal:\n- !!<format: text/x-plantuml> |\n  @startmindmap\n  * Pet keeping\n  ** Dogs\n  *** Daily walks\n  *** Consistent training\n  ** Cats\n  *** Vertical space\n  *** A clean litter box\n  ** Fish\n  *** Water quality\n  *** Sparing feeding\n  @endmindmap\n- *: dogs\n- *: cats\n- *: fish\n- |\n  **Whatever shares your home**, the craft is the same: notice what it needs before it has to\n  ask. Return to the chapter above whenever a new question arrives — the animals are patient\n  teachers.\n\"cover-paw.png\":\n  .yo:\n    thumbnails:\n      [256, 256]: *: .yo: thumbnails: xxh64-429a227f097399ce-256x256.jpg\n",
